From: Stefano Viola <stefano.viola@toradex.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: monaco-arduino-monza: power the Wi-Fi/BT module

The QCA2066 Wi-Fi/Bluetooth module stays off: no PCIe device on pcie1
and the Bluetooth driver times out reading the QCA version. Arduino's
images hog TLMM GPIO 54 (module enable, rfkill) and GPIO 56 (PCIe
always-on supply) high. Do the same, so the module is powered before
the PCIe links are trained at probe.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [stopgap until meta-qcom-arduino's QCA2066 power-sequencing support (PR #22, main) reaches wrynose]
Signed-off-by: Stefano Viola <stefano.viola@toradex.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts
@@ -472,6 +472,25 @@
 };
 
 &tlmm {
+	/*
+	 * Power the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth module (QCA2066) at boot, before the PCIe
+	 * links are trained at probe: module enable (rfkill) and PCIe always-on
+	 * supply, as on Arduino's images.
+	 */
+	wlan-rfkill-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <54 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+		line-name = "wlan-rfkill";
+	};
+
+	wireless-pcie-ao-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <56 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+		line-name = "wireless-pcie-ao";
+	};
+
 	pcie0_default_state: pcie0-default-state {
 		wake-pins {
 			pins = "gpio0";
